        skos:definition        "A miniature data logger that records temperature at a user programmed time interval. 12-bit version gives a resolution of 0.015C and an accuracy of +-0.1C. It is housed in a waterproof cylinder and the temperature sensor is mounted on a protruding stainless steel probe. Further information may be found on the BODC document server at URL: http://www.bodc.ac.uk/data/documents/nodb/108661/"@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0105";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Vemco Minilog12 temperature recorder"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/TEMPPR01/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00348/> .

